// M5-A3P-1010. Ch20 U00 "Down the eye" (C, 2 min). act3_ch20.md §2 U00; rule 6.
// The Kite on Liss's dive rig, sails furled, dropping down the well; every held light the storm has taken hangs in the
// walls of water like a night sky turned inside out (held: no motion). LISS SPENDS TOBIN'S LAMP (ending_cost_audit §4):
// she stops trying to mend it and seats it in the engine socket; his held light is part of the last full charge that
// takes them down. One line (the Ch14 talk, turned). Kerrid is first off the Kite onto the first floor (ADR 0020).
title: ch20_down_the_eye
location: ch20/undertow_layers
---
@letterbox on
@camera U01
@music undertow_descent fade=2.0
@vfx glimmer_held at=well_walls count=200 drift=down_seaward rate=slow
@wait 5.0
@camera U02
@mark liss engine_socket walk
@anim liss open lamp_box
@wait 3.0
@anim liss seat cracked_lamp
@vfx glimmer_bound at=engine_socket count=1
@sfx lamp_seat
@wait 3.0
Liss [grief]: He volunteered. So nobody'd have to be chosen. #line:ch20_eye_001
@wait 4.0
@camera U03
@sfx kite_engine_strains
@wait 4.0
@sfx kite_touches_floor
@mark kerrid first_floor walk
@wait 3.0
<<set $ch20_started = true>>
@letterbox off
===
